  "explanation": "The proposal introduces an integrated framework combining multi-agent dialogue loops with latent-space novelty probing to steer scientific idea generation. While the conceptual idea is compelling, the proposed methodology presents severe technical bottlenecks under the given constraints: extracting internal hidden states and training lightweight probes requires direct white-box access to model activations, which is impossible or cost-prohibitive when using proprietary APIs (such as GPT-4) and extremely memory-intensive when running local 70B open-weights models on a single 12GB consumer GPU. Even with an 8B model, managing hidden-state extractions alongside multi-agent generation loops within a 6-week window exceeds standard resource limits.",
  "problems": [
    "Probing internal hidden states is incompatible with black-box API access and highly memory-intensive for local models on a 12GB consumer GPU.",
    "Training latent probes requires collecting activation datasets and fitting linear classifiers, adding significant implementation complexity for a 6-week project timeline.",
    "Integrating latent-space intervention dynamically into standard multi-agent orchestration frameworks lacks off-the-shelf support and requires custom decoding engineering."
  ],
  "improvements": [
    "Replace hidden-state latent probing with prompt-based or activation-free critique signals (e.g., using explicit text-based novelty scores from a retriever) to avoid white-box access requirements.",
    "Restrict local execution strictly to small-scale open-weights models (e.g., 8B quantized) or entirely to API calls with text-only feedback loops.",
    "Scope the evaluation to a narrower computer science subdomain or subset of RINoBench to fit the 6-week timeline."
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "passage_id": "s_5b01ecf103c7c8a53854",
      "claim": "Probing latent judgments from hidden states requires white-box model access.",
      "relation": "context"
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "s_7e71597111cf2fd6cb3f",
      "claim": "RINoBench dataset is publicly available for evaluation.",
      "relation": "supports"
    }
  ],
  "uncertainty": "The feasibility score assumes local execution of 8B/70B models or API usage under standard 12GB VRAM consumer hardware constraints, where hidden-state extraction for probing is either infeasible or severely constrained by memory limits."
}
